  "interpretation": {
    "scope": "Uniform, prepacked valid rows on one H100; one original request of 512 rows per expert versus two sequential calls of 256 rows per expert. No communication, contention or distributed scheduling.",
    "132_sm_capacity_hint": "Splitting raises full FFN time by 11.8%; projection calls explain most of the increase. This establishes an intrinsic split cost, not the entire distributed regression.",
    "hints": "No consistent advantage from fixing the expected-row hint to 256 or 512; prior distributed traces selected the same kernel templates. This fixed-order single session is not a statistical hint-tuning study.",
    "sm_budget": "132 SMs is fastest for the isolated full FFN. Reducing compute SMs can still affect communication overlap and requires an end-to-end experiment.",
    "limitations": "Independent phase graphs have different cache states and are not an additive budget. Uniform alignment-friendly rows do not model skew or extra partial tiles from independently partitioned routes. All repeat samples are retained."
  },
